      description: "Famciclovir is an oral prodrug rapidly converted to penciclovir, a guanosine analogue activated preferentially in HSV- or VZV-infected cells. Penciclovir triphosphate has a long intracellular half-life and competitively inhibits viral DNA polymerase, slowing viral genome elongation. Unlike acyclovir triphosphate, incorporated penciclovir is not an obligate immediate chain terminator because it retains a 3-prime hydroxyl group, but DNA synthesis still becomes inefficient. This distinction explains how related drugs can share thymidine-kinase resistance yet differ in intracellular persistence. Famciclovir works best when started early in a recurrence because it can stop new replication but cannot erase latency or reverse established neural injury.",
